1
00:00:06,700 --> 00:00:11,990
A pastry recipe uses 0.5 kilograms of flour and 250 grams of butter.

2
00:00:12,040 --> 00:00:17,010
Another recipe uses flour and butter in the ratio 3 to 2.

3
00:00:17,060 --> 00:00:19,050
Which recipe is more buttery?

4
00:00:19,100 --> 00:00:22,360
Pause the video and choose.

5
00:00:22,410 --> 00:00:24,690
Change to the same units.

6
00:00:24,740 --> 00:00:27,200
0.5 kilograms is 500 grams.

7
00:00:27,250 --> 00:00:32,780
So recipe 1 is 500 to 250, which simplifies to 2 to 1.

8
00:00:32,830 --> 00:00:36,930
Recipe 1 has 2 parts of flour for each part of butter.

9
00:00:36,980 --> 00:00:39,930
Recipe 2 has 3 to 2, which is 1.5 to 1.

10
00:00:39,980 --> 00:00:45,410
Less flour for each part of butter, so recipe 2 is more buttery.

11
00:00:45,460 --> 00:00:52,350
Remember: to simplify a ratio, divide all the parts by their highest common factor.

12
00:00:52,400 --> 00:00:54,860
12 to 18 simplifies to 2 to 3.

13
00:00:54,910 --> 00:00:57,920
45 to 60 simplifies to 3 to 4.

14
00:00:57,970 --> 00:01:02,780
If the units are different, change them to the same units first.

15
00:01:02,830 --> 00:01:06,960
To compare ratios, write them in the form n to 1, or 1 to n.

16
00:01:07,010 --> 00:01:09,600
Then they are easy to compare.

17
00:01:09,650 --> 00:01:10,420
Your turn.

18
00:01:10,470 --> 00:01:13,520
Simplify 400 metres to 1.2 kilometres.

19
00:01:13,570 --> 00:01:17,130
Pause the video and try it.

20
00:01:17,180 --> 00:01:20,730
1.2 kilometres is 1,200 metres.

21
00:01:20,780 --> 00:01:22,230
400 to 1,200.

22
00:01:22,280 --> 00:01:25,920
Divide both by 400: 1 to 3.

23
00:01:25,970 --> 00:01:28,620
Clear decimals by multiplying.

24
00:01:28,670 --> 00:01:32,670
1.2 to 0.8 is 12 to 8, which is 3 to 2.

25
00:01:32,720 --> 00:01:36,720
Clear fractions by multiplying by a common denominator.

26
00:01:36,770 --> 00:01:40,070
A half to a third, times 6, is 3 to 2.

27
00:01:40,120 --> 00:01:43,910
Three-part ratios simplify in the same way.

28
00:01:43,960 --> 00:01:48,570
24 to 36 to 60, divided by 12, is 2 to 3 to 5.

29
00:01:48,620 --> 00:01:49,910
Here is the method.

30
00:01:49,960 --> 00:01:55,410
Step 1: change to the same units, and clear any decimals or fractions.

31
00:01:55,460 --> 00:01:58,930
Step 2: divide all the parts by the H C F.

32
00:01:58,980 --> 00:02:04,370
Step 3: to compare, write each ratio in the form 1 to n, or n to 1.

33
00:02:04,420 --> 00:02:08,930
Step 4: keep the parts in the same order as the question.

34
00:02:08,980 --> 00:02:11,650
Simplify 3 quarters to 2 thirds.

35
00:02:11,700 --> 00:02:14,580
Multiply both by 12: 9 to 8.

36
00:02:14,630 --> 00:02:15,420
Your turn.

37
00:02:15,470 --> 00:02:17,110
Simplify 0.6 to 1.5.

38
00:02:17,160 --> 00:02:20,360
Pause and work it out.

39
00:02:20,410 --> 00:02:22,680
Multiply by 10: 6 to 15.

40
00:02:22,730 --> 00:02:25,170
Divide by 3: 2 to 5.

41
00:02:25,220 --> 00:02:29,700
A map's scale is 4 centimetres to 1 kilometre.

42
00:02:29,750 --> 00:02:31,570
Write it as 1 to n.

43
00:02:31,620 --> 00:02:35,020
1 kilometre is 100,000 centimetres.

44
00:02:35,070 --> 00:02:37,180
So it is 4 to 100,000.

45
00:02:37,230 --> 00:02:40,190
Divide by 4: 1 to 25,000.

46
00:02:40,240 --> 00:02:43,190
Class A has 12 boys and 18 girls.

47
00:02:43,240 --> 00:02:46,180
Class B has 10 boys and 14 girls.

48
00:02:46,230 --> 00:02:48,810
Which has more girls per boy?

49
00:02:48,860 --> 00:02:51,260
A: 18 divided by 12 is 1.5.

50
00:02:51,310 --> 00:02:53,710
B: 14 divided by 10 is 1.4.

51
00:02:53,760 --> 00:02:54,990
Class A.

52
00:02:55,040 --> 00:02:58,240
Jo simplifies 300 grams to 2 kilograms.

53
00:02:58,290 --> 00:03:00,450
Which line is wrong?

54
00:03:00,500 --> 00:03:01,770
Line 1 is wrong.

55
00:03:01,820 --> 00:03:03,590
She ignored the units.

56
00:03:03,640 --> 00:03:08,840
Change to the same units first: 300 grams to 2,000 grams.

57
00:03:08,890 --> 00:03:11,960
Divide by 100: 3 to 20.

58
00:03:12,010 --> 00:03:14,510
Screens are described by ratios.

59
00:03:14,560 --> 00:03:16,660
A widescreen TV is 16 to 9.

60
00:03:16,710 --> 00:03:19,050
An older TV was 4 to 3.

61
00:03:19,100 --> 00:03:25,790
In the form n to 1, 16 to 9 is about 1.78 to 1, and 4 to 3 is about 1.33 to 1.

62
00:03:25,840 --> 00:03:30,060
So widescreen is much wider for its height.

63
00:03:30,110 --> 00:03:31,340
One last question.

64
00:03:31,390 --> 00:03:33,610
Write 5 to 8 in the form 1 to n.

65
00:03:33,660 --> 00:03:34,320
What is n?

66
00:03:34,370 --> 00:03:37,650
Pause the video and answer.

67
00:03:37,700 --> 00:03:39,670
Divide both parts by 5.

68
00:03:39,720 --> 00:03:41,610
8 divided by 5 is 1.6.

69
00:03:41,660 --> 00:03:43,750
So it is 1 to 1.6.

70
00:03:43,800 --> 00:03:50,200
To remember: use the same units, clear decimals and fractions, then divide by the H C F.

71
00:03:50,250 --> 00:03:54,080
The forms 1 to n, and n to 1, help you compare.

72
00:03:54,130 --> 00:03:57,120
Three-part ratios work the same way.

73
00:03:57,170 --> 00:03:59,750
Keep the order of the parts.

74
00:03:59,800 --> 00:04:05,190
Great work! Now practise lesson 12.1 on Camday.
